values ('b3c4d5e6-7f8a-4b10-9d00-0e1f2a3b4c10', 'music-history-i-medieval-baroque', 'Music History I (Medieval-Baroque)', 'Music History I surveys music from medieval chant through the high Baroque, emphasizing how repertories were made, notated, performed, circulated, heard, and remembered. Students study chant, early polyphony, medieval secular song, Renaissance sacred and secular music, the rise of opera, Baroque style, Bach, Handel, instrumental forms, and performance practice. The course pairs listening and score study with primary sources, visual/material culture, and historiographical questions so students learn to hear style and think historically.');

